# Upper-air relative humidity (%) — brown = dry air, transparent through
# the neutral middle so the map shows, greens = moist. Unlike rh.clr
# (fire-weather 2m RH, dry-only signal) this shows BOTH tails; used by
# the pressure-level rh* products. interpolate_color smooths it.
nv    0   0   0   0
0     150 100 40  220
20    190 150 90  190
40    220 200 160 120
50    255 255 255 0
60    210 235 200 100
75    150 215 150 170
90    80  180 90  220
100   30  140 60  250
